---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';

const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/privy-vs-attentive';
const title = 'Privy vs Attentive for Shopify: 2026 Comparison';
const desc = "Compare signup capture and coordinated email/SMS launches, rather than assuming Attentive needs a separate capture tool.";

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can Attentive collect Shopify subscribers?",
    "answer": "Yes. Its documentation covers signup units and Shopify email subscriber collection. Confirm the units, channels and journeys available in your account."
  },
  {
    "question": "Must I retain Privy alongside Attentive?",
    "answer": "No. Retain it only if a specific capture or operating requirement justifies the additional system and its handoff."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should decide the choice?",
    "answer": "Rehearse your launch from signup through channel opt-out and purchase exclusion, then compare the complete quotes and operating work."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-[#5d3a1d]">/</span>
        <span class="text-[#5d3a1d]">Privy vs Attentive</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Privy vs Attentive for Shopify</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Compare signup capture and coordinated email/SMS launches, rather than assuming Attentive needs a separate capture tool.</p>
      </header>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Start with the launch you need to coordinate</h2>
        <p>A fashion store preparing a limited release needs a signup offer, an email announcement, and an optional SMS reminder with clear channel permissions. This is a proposed evaluation scenario, not a merchant case study. Privy markets email, SMS and list growth together. Attentive also documents signup units and email subscriber collection for Shopify. Neither should be excluded from capture evaluation on category labels alone.</p>
        <h2>Rehearse the waitlist before the drop</h2>
        <p>Draft a mobile signup journey for an unavailable size. Record the product interest separately from general newsletter consent. Preview the offer, confirmation and first message on the devices your visitors use. An email-only subscriber must not enter the SMS audience merely because a phone number exists on an order. Ask each vendor to show how signup source and channel permission reach the journey audience.</p>
        <h2>Choose one owner for each announcement</h2>
        <p>Map the release email, early-access text and public-sale reminder. If you retain another email platform, assign each message to exactly one system. During a proposed rehearsal, opt out of text while retaining email, then purchase before the reminder. Check the audience exclusions in every sending system. A documented integration is not evidence that your particular suppression rule has propagated.</p>
        <h2>Measure incremental value rather than channel credit</h2>
        <p>A shopper can click an email and a text before buying. Adding both dashboards can double-count the same order. If your traffic permits a meaningful experiment, define a holdout and the observation window before launch. Compare order contribution after discounts, message charges and returns. Without a valid comparison group, report attributed sales as attribution rather than claiming incremental lift.</p>
        <h2>Price the actual channel mix</h2>
        <p>Request written quotes covering the intended email audience, SMS destinations, message types, usage, onboarding, support and renewal conditions. Include your existing email system if it remains. Model a release month separately from an ordinary month. There is no store-revenue or SMS-revenue percentage that universally makes Attentive affordable or Privy mandatory.</p>
        <h2>Make the operating handoff reviewable</h2>
        <p>Give the release operator an audience map, consent-field definitions and a pause procedure. Rehearse changing the VIP group and excluding recent buyers before enabling customer messages. Obtain jurisdiction-specific review of the final signup and messaging program; platform features do not establish legal compliance. No live launch or product test was performed for this comparison.</p>
        <h2>Decision</h2>
        <p>Shortlist either product if it can cover your required capture and messaging path. Prefer the configuration your team can operate with explicit permissions and a supportable total cost. A combined stack can be reasonable when an existing email program must remain, but keeping Privy solely because Attentive supposedly lacks capture would rest on a false premise.</p>
        <h2>Primary documentation</h2>
        <p>Product scope checked against primary material on November 25, 2026. Documentation establishes advertised capabilities, not results for this store.</p>
        <ul><li><a class="link" href="https://www.privy.com/">Privy product scope</a></li><li><a class="link" href="https://help.attentive.com/hc/en-us/articles/6376556345876-Get-started-with-sign-up-units">Attentive signup units</a></li><li><a class="link" href="https://help.attentive.com/hc/en-us/articles/4434114124564-Collect-email-subscribers-from-Shopify">Shopify email collection</a></li></ul>
      </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-attentive">Omnisend vs Attentive</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/privy-vs-postscript">Privy vs Postscript</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/fashion">Email apps for fashion stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Privy vs Attentive FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
